olic, Baptist, Congregational New Church, Methodist, Presbyterian","ordinal":35,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:35","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"people-and-society","label":"Languages","content":"English 94.5% (official), Portuguese 4.6%, other 0.9% (2001 census)","ordinal":36,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:36","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"people-and-society","label":"Literacy","content":"definition: NA\n\ntotal population: NA%\n\nmale: NA%\n\nfemale: NA%","ordinal":37,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:37","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Country name","content":"conventional long form: Bailiwick of Jersey\n\nconventional short form: Jersey","ordinal":38,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:38","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Dependency status","content":"British crown dependency","ordinal":39,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:39","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Government type","content":"NA","ordinal":40,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:40","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Capital","content":"Saint Helier","ordinal":41,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:41","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Administrative divisions","content":"none (British crown dependency)","ordinal":42,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:42","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Independence","content":"none (British crown dependency)","ordinal":43,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:43","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"National holiday","content":"Liberation Day, 9 May (1945)","ordinal":44,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:44","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Constitution","content":"unwritten; partly statutes, partly common law and practice","ordinal":45,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:45","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Legal system","content":"English law and local statute; justice is administered by the Royal Court","ordinal":46,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:46","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Suffrage","content":"NA years of age; universal adult","ordinal":47,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:47","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Executive branch","content":"chief of state: Queen ELIZABETH II (since 6 February 1952)\n\nhead of government: Lieutenant Governor and Commander in Chief Air Chief Marshall Sir John CHESHIRE (since 24 January 2001) and Bailiff Philip Martin BAILHACHE (since NA February 1995)\n\ncabinet: committees appointed by the Assembly of the States\n\nelections: none; the monarch is hereditary; lieutenant governor and bailiff appointed by the monarch","ordinal":48,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:48","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Legislative branch","content":"unicameral Assembly of the States (55 voting members - 12 senators (elected for 6-year terms), 12 constables or heads of parishes (elected for 3-year terms), 29 deputies (elected for 3-year terms); the bailiff and the deputy bailiff; and 3 non-voting members - the Dean of Jersey, the Attorney General, and the Solicitor General all appointed by the monarch)\n\nelections: last held NA (next to be held NA)\n\nelection results: percent of vote - NA%; seats - independents 53","ordinal":49,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:49","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Judicial branch","content":"Royal Court (judges elected by an electoral college and the bailiff)","ordinal":50,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:50","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Political parties and leaders","content":"none; all independents","ordinal":51,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:51","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Political pressure groups and leaders","content":"none","ordinal":52,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:52","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation in the US","content":"none (British crown dependency)","ordinal":53,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:53","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation from the US","content":"none (British crown dependency)","ordinal":54,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:54","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"government","label":"Flag description","content":"white with a diagonal red cross extending to the corners of the flag; in the upper quadrant, surmounted by a yellow crown, a red shield with the three lions of England in yellow","ordinal":55,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:55","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"Economy - overview","content":"The Channel Island economy is based on international financial services, agriculture, and tourism. In 1996 the finance sector accounted for about 60% of the island's output. Potatoes, cauliflower, tomatoes, and especially flowers are important export crops, shipped mostly to the UK. The Jersey breed of dairy cattle is known worldwide and represents an important export income earner. Milk products go to the UK and other EU countries. Tourism accounts for 24% of GDP. In recent years, the government has encouraged light industry to locate in Jersey, with the result that an electronics industry has developed alongside the traditional manufacturing of knitwear. All raw material and energy requirements are imported, as well as a large share of Jersey's food needs. Light taxes and death duties make the island a popular tax haven. Living standards come close to those of the UK.","ordinal":56,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:56","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (purchasing power parity)","content":"$3.6 billion (2003 est.)","ordinal":57,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:57","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - real growth rate","content":"NA%","ordinal":58,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:58","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - per capita","content":"purchasing power parity - $40,000 (2003 est.)","ordinal":59,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:59","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - composition by sector","content":"agriculture: 5%\n\nindustry: 2%\n\nservices: 93% (1996)","ordinal":60,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:60","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"Labor force","content":"52,790 (2004)","ordinal":61,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:61","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"Unemployment rate","content":"0.9% (2004 est.)","ordinal":62,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:62","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"Population below poverty line","content":"NA%","ordinal":63,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:63","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"Household income or consumption by percentage share","content":"lowest 10%: NA%\n\nhighest 10%: NA%","ordinal":64,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:64","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"Inflation rate (consumer prices)","content":"5.3% (2004)","ordinal":65,"locator":"factbook-2005/geos/je.html#field:65","country":"JE","edition_year":2005},{"category":"economy","label":"Budget","content":"rev